      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Thrissur</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When a Two‑Wheeler or Motorcycle arrives at its destination, the delivery handover follows a strict, step‑by‑step protocol designed to guarantee that the asset is returned in the exact condition it was handed out. The process begins with a daylight re‑inspection, proceeds to odometer verification, and concludes with a signed condition sign‑off.</p>
<p>Each phase is documented, photographed, and cross‑checked against the original pickup records to provide full audit trail integrity.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑Inspection</strong>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>All visible surfaces—body panels, frame, wheels, and paint—are examined under natural light to detect any new scratches, dents, or paint chips.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Photographs are taken from the same angles as the pickup images, ensuring a side‑by‑side visual comparison. Any discrepancies are logged immediately.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Functional tests (e.g., brake lever, clutch, ignition) are performed to confirm that the motorcycle operates as it did at the time of pickup.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>All findings are recorded in the delivery checklist and attached to the final report.</span></li>
</ul>
</span></li>

<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Odometer Verification Against LR Bilty</strong>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The mileage reading on the motorcycle’s odometer is captured with a calibrated camera and compared directly to the mileage noted on the LR bilty issued at pickup.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Any deviation beyond the acceptable variance threshold (typically ±5 km) triggers a mandatory investigation, which may involve a third‑party mileage audit.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Both the rider’s signature and the transporter’s signature are required on the mileage confirmation slip to validate the reading.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Discrepancies are documented in the delivery log and communicated to the operations manager for follow‑up.</span></li>
</ul>
</span></li>

<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑Off</strong>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>After the re‑inspection and odometer check, the recipient signs the delivery receipt, confirming that the motorcycle is in the agreed condition.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The transporter’s representative also signs, acknowledging the recipient’s acceptance and the completion of the handover.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Both signatures are scanned and stored in the electronic asset management system, linking them to the corresponding inspection photos and mileage data.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The signed receipt is returned to the dispatch office within 24 hours, closing the delivery cycle and triggering any necessary post‑delivery actions.</span></li>
</ul>
</span></li>
</ul>

<p>By rigorously following these steps, the organization ensures that every Two‑Wheeler or Motorcycle is delivered and returned with full accountability, preserving asset value and fostering trust with all stakeholders.</p></div>
